%description:

The indoor distance d2D-in of a UE under TR 38.901's multi-carrier O2I model,
through the real PHY: the minimum of two uniform draws, with a range that
depends on the scenario. The model deviates (model-deviations item 17): it
draws one uniform in [0, 25) m in every scenario. CellularRadioIndoorDraw pins
what the radio draws, so that this test fails on its checks and not on an
abort.

TR 38.901 v16.1.0 7.4.3.1, for the O2I models of Table 7.4.3-2: "d2D-in is
minimum of two independently generated uniformly distributed variables between
0 and 25 m for UMa and UMi-Street Canyon, and between 0 and 10 m for RMa. d2D-in
shall be UT-specifically generated." The single-frequency model of Table 7.4.3-3
(UMa and UMi below 6 GHz) takes "a single, link-specific, uniformly distributed
variable between 0 and 25 m" instead; IndoorOneRadioTwoCarriers covers that.

Real NrUe and gNodeB nodes run on one carrier at 28 GHz, where Table 7.4.3-2
applies in UMa, and in RMa, which has the low-loss model of that table at every
frequency. 256 UEs stand at one place, 60 m from the base station, indoors and
outdoors, with a fixed LOS state, and fading, shadowing and interference off.
Outdoors minus indoors, a UE's measured DL SINR is its O2I loss:

    PL_tw + 0.5 d2D-in + 4.4 z,   PL_tw = 5 - 10 log10(0.3 10^(-L_glass/10) + 0.7 10^(-L_concrete/10))

with z the UE's standard normal deviate (sigma_P = 4.4 dB, low-loss model).
So (SINR_outdoor - SINR_indoor - PL_tw) / 0.5 is d2D-in + 8.8 z, and its mean
over the UEs estimates the mean of d2D-in: L/3 for the minimum of two uniforms
in [0, L), where one uniform has L/2. The mean is graded against L/3, 8.33 m in
UMa and 3.33 m in RMa, to within 4 standard errors (sqrt(L^2/18 + 8.8^2) /
sqrt(256): 2.6 m in UMa, 2.3 m in RMa). One uniform in [0, 25) gives 12.5 m.

%expected-failure: an indoor UE's d2D-in is one uniform in [0, 25) m, where TR 38.901 7.4.3.1 takes the minimum of two, in [0, 25) m for UMa and [0, 10) m for RMa

%extraargs: -c IndoorDistanceSpec

%file: demo.xml
<config>
    <interface among='eNB* eNodeB* enb* *Enb* gNB* gNodeB* gnb* *Gnb* upf* *Upf* mecHost* pgw*' address='10.x.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
    <interface hosts='*' address='192.168.x.x' netmask='255.255.x.x'/>
</config>

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[Config IndoorDistanceSpec]
network = simu5g.simulations.nr.networks.SingleCell_Standalone

# the positions this test gives the nodes are their antennas': no height offset
**.antenna.mobility.offsetZ = 0m
sim-time-limit = 0.1s
**.routingRecorder.enabled = false
cmdenv-express-mode = true
cmdenv-status-frequency = 10000000s
seed-set = 0

output-scalar-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.sca
output-vector-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.vec
**.vector-recording = false

############### The sweep ##############
*.ue[*].**.insideBuilding = ${indoor = false, true}
*.gnb.cellularNic.radio.scenario = ${scenario = "URBAN_MACROCELL", "RURAL_MACROCELL"}

############### One carrier at 28 GHz, under TR 38.901 ##############
*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 1
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 28GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 6
*.radioMedium.nrChannelModelType = "Tr38901ChannelModel"

############### Geometry: every UE at one place, below the breakpoint distance ##############
*.gnb.mobility.initialX = 300m
*.gnb.mobility.initialY = 300m
*.gnb.mobility.initialZ = 25m
*.numUe = 256
*.ue[*].servingNodeId = 0
*.ue[*].nrServingNodeId = 1
*.ue[*].mobility.initialX = 360m
*.ue[*].mobility.initialY = 300m
*.ue[*].mobility.initialZ = 1.5m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinX = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinY = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinZ = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxX = 1000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxY = 1000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxZ = 50m
**.mobility.initFromDisplayString = false

############### The channel: one path loss and the indoor loss ##############
**.dynamicLos = false
**.fixedLos = true
**.fading = false
**.shadowing = false
**.downlinkInterference = false
**.uplinkInterference = false
**.bgCellInterference = false
**.extCellInterference = false

*.configurator.config = xmldoc("./demo.xml")

%postrun-command: ../../physics_reference.py --grade results >verdict.txt

%contains: verdict.txt
graded=2 failures=0

%not-contains: verdict.txt
FAILED
